  "paired_inference": "Independent unit is the maze; joint success requires all three fixed models. For each paired-net endpoint use exact Clopper-Pearson gain and loss marginal one-sided alpha .025 each, lower=100*(gain_lower-loss_upper), upper=100*(gain_upper-loss_lower). Support if lower >= declared threshold; falsify if upper < threshold; else inconclusive. Regression-probability endpoint uses exact paired-loss count over4096 with one-sided alpha .05: support if upper<=.1pp, falsify if lower>.1pp, else inconclusive. Five separate endpoint decisions; no simultaneous familywise95 claim. With zero losses/4096 the upper probability bound is .0731113pp. NI concerns net accuracy, not standalone loss probability. The absolute sufficiency endpoint uses a one-sided alpha.05 Clopper-Pearson interval directly on joint successes/4096: support if lower>=99.9%, falsify if upper<99.9%, otherwise inconclusive. Each of the five endpoints has its own decision; no simultaneous familywise95 claim.",
